	<h2><font face="Tahoma">Fraud Protection</font></h2>
<p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">While the vast majority of Player Auctions
transactions are trouble-free, be aware that Fraud can happen. Here's how fraud
is defined on Player Auctions:</font>
<ol>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Paying for an item and never receiving it or</font>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Receiving an item that is less than what is
    described -- such as winning a solid gold ring at auction but receiving a
    copper one instead.</font></li>
</ol>
<p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">What steps can be taken to help protect you?</font></p>
<ol>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Items listed on this site are most often
    posted by individuals, and sometimes small companies. While we try and
    regulate our site and remove objectionable material or listings, we cannot
    be responsible for regulating or verifying every item for sale. You need to
    be aware of the potential for misleading statements or fraud of a listed
    item, or the possibility of purchasing an illegal product.</font></li>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">You can minimize your risk by e-mailing the
    seller with specific questions related to the item and checking out the
    seller's feedback report compiled by other individuals who have purchased
    from this person/company. </font><font color="#333333" face="Tahoma" size="2">Always
    take note of a users feedback, take the time to read over all the users
    feedback and all the comments that are left as well as who is leaving the
    feedback.</font></li>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Also, consider using safe, easy-to-use escrow
    services at the end of auction. <a href="http://www.playerauctions.com/help/faqIEscrow.cfm">Escrow
    services</a>, such as <a href="http://www.iescrow.com/beyondsolutions/">i-Escrow</a>,
    provide security by keeping custody of your funds and releasing them to the
    seller only when specified conditions are met.</font></li>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Consider always paying with your Credit
    Card Card (Paypal and other such programs use your credit card). If by
    chance your auction is not delivered you can contact your bank or the
    program you used such as Paypal to have the charges reversed. Paying with a
    money order or Western Union can always be hazardous as there is no
    Guarantee of delivery or retrieval of lost funds.</font></li>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Consider only buying from users who use <a href="http://www.squaretrade.com/learnmore/seal_092100.jsp?1171">SquareTrade</a>
    or other such programs. <a href="http://www.squaretrade.com/learnmore/seal_092100.jsp?1171">SquareTrade</a><font color="#333333">
    stands by its members - Fraud Protection Guarantee covers buyers up to $250.</font></font></li>
  <li><font color="#333333" face="Tahoma" size="2">Check our <a href="http://www.playerauctions.com/forums/categories.cfm?catid=8">Fraud
    Report board</a> to make sure you do not see this seller listed as a fraudulent
    user.</font></li>
</ol>
<p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">What can I do if I was the victim of a <font color="#333333">fraudulent
user?</font></font></p>
<ol>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">First, try to communicate with your seller
    directly. Many problems are just simple misunderstandings.</font></li>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">If after two weeks you have not received your
    auction or gotten a refund please send us a email at <a href="mailto:pasupport@playerauctions.com">pasupport@playerauctions.com</a>
    and include the following.<br>
    A. Your username, full name, email address and telephone number<br>
    B. Auction number of the auction in question<br>
    C. Username of the person in question<br>
    D. A full account of what has transpired as well as any emails.<br>
    In the event PlayerAuctions.com, in its
    sole discretion, determines by any means or proceedings that any User has
    provided false, misleading or illegal activity, PlayerAuctions.com may
    suspend or terminate the User account.</font></li>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Leave negative feedback on user in question,
    all users with a negative three feedback rating will be removed.</font></li>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Leave a post on our <font color="#333333"><a href="http://www.playerauctions.com/forums/categories.cfm?catid=8">Fraud
    Report board</a> to help warn other users about this person.</font></font></li>
  <li><font color="#333333" face="Tahoma" size="2">If you paid using your credit
    card please contact your bank immediately to have the charges
    reversed, if you used Paypal or any other such payment method please contact
    them as well to dispute the charge and to have it reversed.</font></li>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">We encourage you to report all user-to-user
    disputes to your local law enforcement, postmaster general, or a certified
    mediation or arbitration entity.</font></li>
  <li><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Buyers and sellers can also use dispute
    resolution through <a href="http://www.squaretrade.com/learnmore/seal_092100.jsp?1171">SquareTrade</a>,
    an independent, neutral third party to help resolve disputes that may arise.
  <li>Report fraudulent users to the <a href="http://www.ifccfbi.gov">Internet Fraud Complaint Center</a>. 
<br><br><b>
The Internet Fraud Complaint Center (IFCC) is a partnership between the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) and the National White Collar Crime Center (NW3C).
<br><br>
IFCC's mission is to address fraud committed over the Internet. For victims of Internet fraud, IFCC provides a convenient and easy-to-use reporting mechanism that alerts authorities of a suspected criminal or civil violation. For law enforcement and regulatory agencies at all levels, IFCC offers a central repository for complaints related to Internet fraud, works to quantify fraud patterns, and provides timely statistical data of current fraud trends.</b>
<br><br>
Fraudulent users who take advantage of people using U.S. money orders or Western Union can face time in jail while those living outside the U.S. can forever lose their right to step on U.S. soil. Please take the time to report all fraudulent users to <a href="http://www.ifccfbi.gov/default.asp">IFCC</a> so we can help put an end to all such activity.
</font></li>
</ol>
<p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Please read our </font><font face="Tahoma" size="2"><a href="http://www.playerauctions.com/registration/user_agreement.cfm">User
 Agreement</a> very carefully and fully understand it before using our
site.<br>
<br>
All users who are caught taking part in </font><font color="#333333" face="Tahoma" size="2">fraudulent
activity on Player Auctions will be prosecuted to the full extent of the law.<br>
Using a anonymous email such as hotmail or yahoo will not protect users from
being tracked down. Player Auctions logs all IP info and using this info can
track users down fairly quickly. Player Auctions will hold fraudulent users
liable for all costs of attorney fees as well as any hidden costs for time taken
to track them down. Fraudulent activity is illegal in the United States and violators
will be prosecuted to the full extent of the law. In the case a fraudulent user
is under the age of 18, the parents or guardian of the user will be held
accountable for all such costs.<br>
<br>
Thank You<br>
Player Auctions</font></p>
